{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CbvpZu6uSBBC3HQpdB9Ubk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Iteration US-162 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n2\t\n3\tCompleted: Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup (ID: US-162)\n4\t\n5\t### What was implemented\n6\t- Created `lib/cache-utils.ts` with two functions:\n7\t  - `getCachedData()`: Generic utility that wraps fetch with cache() and cacheSignal()\n8\t  - `getCachedRoomAvailability()`: Example implementation for room availability API calls\n9\t- Updated `Rooms.tsx` Server Component to import and demonstrate cacheSignal() pattern\n10\t- Added try-catch error handling to gracefully handle AbortError when cache is invalidated\n11\t- No TypeScript errors; all 83 pages generated successfully during build\n12\t\n13\t### Patterns discovered\n14\t- React 19.2 cacheSignal() is only available in Server Components (not Client Components or Route Handlers)\n15\t- cacheSignal() returns an AbortSignal that fires when cache lifetime ends\n16\t- Pattern: `const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() }))`\n17\t- AbortError has name property that can be checked to distinguish cache invalidation from network errors\n18\t- Graceful error handling prevents cache-related aborts from breaking the page\n19\t\n20\t### Gotchas\n21\t- cacheSignal() is a React 19.2 feature; requires Next.js 16+ for full support\n22\t- Must import both `cache` and `cacheSignal` from \"react\" (not from \"next/cache\")\n23\t- External API calls may fail during SSR (expected for example APIs) — always wrap in try-catch\n24\t\n25\t## Iteration US-161 (Attempt 3) - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n26\t\n27\tCompleted: Implement React 19.2 useEffectEvent for stable analytics event handlers (ID: US-161)\n28\t\n29\t### What was implemented\n30\t- Replaced `useCallback` with `useEffectEvent` in RoomsEcommerceTracker.tsx and BookEcommerceTracker.tsx\n31\t- Removed analytics click handlers from useEffect dependency arrays\n32\t- Effects now run once on mount, not on every callback identity change\n33\t\n34\t### Patterns discovered\n35\t- Code was already committed in attempt 2 (d9fa754) but diff guard failed due to unstaged files inflating diff count\n36\t- Attempt 3 only needed to verify code was in place and mark passes: true\n37\t- When prior attempts commit code but fail post-commit gates, verify existing commits before re-implementing\n38\t\n39\t### Gotchas\n40\t- SPIRAL diff guard counts ALL staged/unstaged changes, not just story-related files — always use `git add <specific-files>` not `git add -A`\n41\t- Previous attempts failed at 540 and 23068 lines because unrelated modified files were included in the diff measurement\n42\t\n43\t## Iteration US-144 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n44\t\n45\tCompleted: Replace JavaScript tooltip positioning with CSS Popover API and Anchor Positioning (ID: US-144)\n46\t\n47\t### What was implemented\n48\t- Created `InfoPopover.tsx` component using native HTML `popover` attribute, `popoverTarget`, CSS `anchor-name`/`position-anchor`\n49\t- Added popover + anchor positioning CSS in globals.css with `@supports` fallback for browsers without anchor positioning\n50\t- Converted Header.tsx search button `title` tooltip to InfoPopover\n51\t- Converted HeroTrustBadges.tsx trust badge buttons to InfoPopover with contextual content\n52\t- No JS tooltip library existed to remove (no Popper.js/Floating UI in the project)\n53\t\n54\t### Patterns discovered\n55\t- React 19 includes `popover` and `popoverTarget` in its type definitions — no `@ts-expect-error` needed\n56\t- `CSS.escape()` is a browser API not available in Node.js SSR — use regex sanitization instead for `useId()` output\n57\t- Attempt 1 failed with 17,788 line diff — caused by touching package-lock.json or similar large files\n58\t- Keep implementation under 500 lines total insertions+deletions\n59\t\n60\t### Gotchas\n61\t- `useId()` returns colon-wrapped strings like `:r0:` — must sanitize for CSS custom property names\n62\t- Linter may auto-revert changes if import is added separately from usage\n63\t\n64\t## Iteration US-143 (FINAL - Attempt 3) - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n65\t\n66\tCompleted: Apply CSS @starting-style for GPU-accelerated entry animations (ID: US-143)\n67\t\n68\t### What was implemented\n69\t- Added @starting-style CSS utility classes (.entry-fade, .entry-zoom-in, .entry-fade-up) to globals.css\n70\t- Classes use only opacity + transform for GPU compositor thread\n71\t- Includes prefers-reduced-motion: reduce override that disables transitions\n72\t- Components modified in commit b3c2354: CookieConsent, ExitIntentOverlay, RoomsTabsClient, SearchDialog\n73\t- CSS classes added in commit 9d11b13\n74\t\n75\t### Patterns discovered\n76\t- Attempt 1 failed: oversized diff (14829 lines > 500 limit)\n77\t- Attempt 2 failed: missing diagnosis block (process gate)\n78\t- Attempt 3 succeeded: code was already committed, just needed verification and passes=true\n79\t- When implementation is already committed, verify in-place rather than re-implementing\n80\t\n81\t### Gotchas\n82\t- SPIRAL may revert prd.json passes flag between attempts even if code is committed\n83\t- The TurnstileWidget TS error is pre-existing (missing @marsidev/react-turnstile dep) and unrelated\n84\t- Always output diagnosis block BEFORE any file edits to pass SPIRAL process gate\n85\t\n86\t## Iteration US-249 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n87\t\n88\tCompleted: Blog post - 5 Gig Jobs for Malaysians Waiting for Singapore Work Approval (ID: US-249)\n89\t\n90\t### What was implemented\n91\t- **Blog post** (`site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`):\n92\t  - Added new blog post object with slug `gig-jobs-malaysia-waiting-singapore-work-pass`\n93\t  - Category: \"Career & Work\", date: \"2026-04-14\", readTime: \"9 min read\"\n94\t  - 5 gig economy job options with earnings estimates:\n95\t    - Foodpanda Delivery Rider: RM1,800–3,500/month\n96\t    - Lalamove Driver: RM2,000–3,800/month\n97\t    - Grab Ride/GrabFood Driver: RM2,500–4,200/month\n98\t    - Part-time F&B/Cafe Work: RM1,500–2,500/month\n99\t    - Online Freelancing: RM1,200–5,000+/month\n100\t  - Each job includes: requirements, earnings breakdown, pros, and cons\n101\t  - Sections on combining gigs, tax/legal notes, Pelangi guest relevance\n102\t  - Internal links to `/rooms` (Pelangi Capsule)\n103\t  - Intro references Pelangi guests in work pass waiting period\n104\t\n105\t### Patterns discovered\n106\t- Blog post HTML content needs careful optimization to stay under 8000 character limit\n107\t- Initial draft (8191 chars) required condensing descriptions by ~35% to fit limit\n108\t- Final optimized content: 5315 characters (well within limit)\n109\t- Consistent format: metadata + HTML content with proper spacing and paragraph structure\n110\t\n111\t### Test results\n112\t- Content size: 5315 characters (under 8000 limit) ✓\n113\t- TypeScript compilation: ✓ passes (npx tsc --noEmit)\n114\t- Next.js build: ✓ succeeds (all static pages generated)\n115\t- All internal links present: `/rooms` (2 times) ✓\n116\t- All acceptance criteria met:\n117\t  - ✓ Slug 'gig-jobs-malaysia-waiting-singapore-work-pass', category 'Career & Work'\n118\t  - ✓ 5 gig job options with earnings estimates\n119\t  - ✓ Intro references Pelangi guests\n120\t  - ✓ readTime '9 min read', date '2026-04-14'\n121\t  - ✓ npm run build passes\n122\t\n123\t## Iteration US-244 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n124\t\n125\tCompleted: Blog post - Living in JB Working in Singapore — Cross-Border Commuter Guide 2026 (ID: US-244)\n126\t\n127\t### What was implemented\n128\t- **Blog post** (`site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`):\n129\t  - Added new blog post object with slug `jb-singapore-commuter-guide-2026`\n130\t  - Category: \"Career & Work\", date: \"2026-04-14\", readTime: \"8 min read\"\n131\t  - Comprehensive HTML table of 5 bus services with routes, prices, duration, and frequency:\n132\t    - Causeway Link: RM5–6 / SGD2–2.50\n133\t    - SBS Transit: R