{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VyFbESnaWME26RULESsfwE","type":"tool_result","content":"4200\t        \"Combine with 'Book Direct = Best Price' trust badge story already in PRD\",\n4201\t        \"Rate parity is a prerequisite for Google Hotel Center free booking link eligibility\"\n4202\t      ],\n4203\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n4204\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n4205\t      \"passes\": true\n4206\t    },\n4207\t    {\n4208\t      \"id\": \"US-187\",\n4209\t      \"title\": \"Add CSS native scroll-driven carousel using ::scroll-button() and ::scroll-marker\",\n4210\t      \"priority\": \"low\",\n4211\t      \"description\": \"Chrome 135+ (March 2025) ships native CSS carousels via ::scroll-button() and ::scroll-marker pseudo-elements. These provide automatic ARIA button roles, keyboard handling, and reduced JavaScript dependency. The gallery and room-photo sliders can be refactored to use this zero-JS approach.\",\n4212\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n4213\t        \"Gallery carousel uses scroll-snap CSS with ::scroll-button() for prev/next controls\",\n4214\t        \"::scroll-marker group provides keyboard-accessible dot indicators\",\n4215\t        \"Fallback for non-supporting browsers degrades to scrollable overflow without JS errors\",\n4216\t        \"@supports query wraps the new pseudo-element declarations\",\n4217\t        \"Lighthouse reports no layout shift (CLS=0) from carousel on load\"\n4218\t      ],\n4219\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n4220\t        \"Chrome 135+ required; use @supports (selector(::scroll-button(*))) guard\",\n4221\t        \"Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/blog/carousels-with-css\",\n4222\t        \"Companion spec: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-5/#scroll-marker-group\"\n4223\t      ],\n4224\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n4225\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n4226\t      \"passes\": false,\n4227\t      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n4228\t    },\n4229\t    {\n4230\t      \"id\": \"US-188\",\n4231\t      \"title\": \"Adopt CSS appearance: base-select for styled native <select> elements\",\n4232\t      \"priority\": \"low\",\n4233\t      \"description\": \"Chrome 130+ (Interop 2025) ships appearance: base-select, allowing the native <select> element to be fully styled with CSS while retaining built-in accessibility semantics. This eliminates the need for custom Radix UI Select components in simple dropdowns, reducing bundle size.\",\n4234\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n4235\t        \"Language switcher and any filter dropdowns use <select> with appearance: base-select where custom Select was used\",\n4236\t        \"Styled select matches brand design system (border-radius, colours, font)\",\n4237\t        \"@supports (appearance: base-select) guard ensures progressive enhancement\",\n4238\t        \"No regression in WCAG 4.1.2 — native select retains keyboard and screen reader support\"\n4239\t      ],\n4240\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n4241\t        \"Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/blog/a-customizable-select\",\n4242\t        \"Polyfill not needed — fallback to system select is acceptable\",\n4243\t        \"Works in Chrome 130+, Safari TP, Firefox Nightly as of 2025\"\n4244\t      ],\n4245\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n4246\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n4247\t      \"passes\": false,\n4248\t      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n4249\t    },\n4250\t    {\n4251\t      \"id\": \"US-189\",\n4252\t      \"title\": \"Use <dialog closedby='any'> for light-dismiss modals without JavaScript\",\n4253\t      \"priority\": \"low\",\n4254\t      \"description\": \"Chrome 133+ adds the closedby attribute to the native <dialog> element, enabling backdrop-click dismiss declaratively without JavaScript event listeners. Reduces bundle size and improves accessibility reliability for cookie consent, gallery lightbox, and booking modals.\",\n4255\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n4256\t        \"Cookie consent, gallery lightbox, and booking confirmation modals use <dialog closedby='any'>\",\n4257\t        \"Escape key closes all dialogs without additional JS handler\",\n4258\t        \"Clicking backdrop closes dialogs where closedby='any' is set\",\n4259\t        \"Progressive enhancement: feature detection used for graceful fallback\",\n4260\t        \"Screen readers announce dialog correctly via native dialog role\"\n4261\t      ],\n4262\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n4263\t        \"Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/blog/dialog-closedby\",\n4264\t        \"Combine with ::backdrop CSS for branded overlay\",\n4265\t        \"Remove duplicate JS click-outside listeners after migration\"\n4266\t      ],\n4267\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n4268\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n4269\t      \"passes\": false,\n4270\t      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n4271\t    },\n4272\t    {\n4273\t      \"id\": \"US-190\",\n4274\t      \"title\": \"Add SiteNavigationElement schema to main navigation for Google Sitelinks\",\n4275\t      \"priority\": \"low\",\n4276\t      \"description\": \"Google Search supports schema.org SiteNavigationElement to understand a site's primary navigation structure. Adding this to the main navigation helps Google understand site hierarchy and can improve Sitelinks display in SERPs for branded searches.\",\n4277\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n4278\t        \"JSON-LD script in layout.tsx includes SiteNavigationElement for all primary nav items\",\n4279\t        \"Each item has @type: SiteNavigationElement, name, and url properties\",\n4280\t        \"Rich Results Test validates the schema without errors\",\n4281\t        \"Navigation items in schema match exactly the visible nav links\"\n4282\t      ],\n4283\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n4284\t        \"Reference: https://schema.org/SiteNavigationElement\",\n4285\t        \"Use ItemList wrapping SiteNavigationElement for ordered nav\",\n4286\t        \"Combine with existing WebSite SearchAction schema in the same JSON-LD block\"\n4287\t      ],\n4288\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n4289\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n4290\t      \"passes\": true\n4291\t    },\n4292\t    {\n4293\t      \"id\": \"US-191\",\n4294\t      \"title\": \"Comply with Malaysia CPETTR 2024 — mandatory Bahasa Malaysia disclosure\",\n4295\t      \"priority\": \"critical\",\n4296\t      \"description\": \"The Consumer Protection (Electronic Trade Transaction) Regulations 2024 came into force on 25 December 2024 and require all information shown to Malaysian consumers in online trade transactions to be available in Bahasa Malaysia. This includes pricing, descriptions, terms and conditions, and mandatory trader identity disclosures (name, address, registration, contact). Non-compliance exposes the business to enforcement under the Consumer Protection Act 1999.\",\n4297\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n4298\t        \"All price displays, room descriptions, booking terms, cancellation policy, and contact details are available in Bahasa Malaysia on the website\",\n4299\t        \"A Bahasa Malaysia toggle or dedicated BM version serves the required content (can be the same page with i18n)\",\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"650472e5-a1e2-490b-836b-3f33e6c52d9d","uuid":"b55ef2dc-47dd-4598-a972-b5b4bb72c3aa","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:09:37.893Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\prd.json","content":"        \"Combine with 'Book Direct = Best Price' trust badge story already in PRD\",\n        \"Rate parity is a prerequisite for Google Hotel Center free booking link eligibility\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-187\",\n      \"title\": \"Add CSS native scroll-driven carousel using ::scroll-button() and ::scroll-marker\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"Chrome 135+ (March 2025) ships native CSS carousels via ::scroll-button() and ::scroll-marker pseudo-elements. These provide automatic ARIA button roles, keyboard handling, and reduced JavaScript dependency. The gallery and room-photo sliders can be refactored to use this zero-JS approach.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Gallery carousel uses scroll-snap CSS with ::scroll-button() for prev/next controls\",\n        \"::scroll-marker group provides keyboard-accessible dot indicators\",\n        \"Fallback for non-supporting browsers degrades to scrollable overflow without JS errors\",\n        \"@supports query wraps the new pseudo-element declarations\",\n        \"Lighthouse reports no layout shift (CLS=0) from carousel on load\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Chrome 135+ required; use @supports (selector(::scroll-button(*))) guard\",\n        \"Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/blog/carousels-with-css\",\n        \"Companion spec: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-5/#scroll-marker-group\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-188\",\n      \"title\": \"Adopt CSS appearance: base-select for styled native <select> elements\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"Chrome 130+ (Interop 2025) ships appearance: base-select, allowing the native <select> element to be fully styled with CSS while retaining built-in accessibility semantics. This eliminates the need for custom Radix UI Select components in simple dropdowns, reducing bundle size.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Language switcher and any filter dropdowns use <select> with appearance: base-select where custom Select was used\",\n        \"Styled select matches brand design system (border-radius, colours, font)\",\n        \"@supports (appearance: base-select) guard ensures progressive enhancement\",\n        \"No regression in WCAG 4.1.2 — native select retains keyboard and screen reader support\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/blog/a-customizable-select\",\n        \"Polyfill not needed — fallback to system select is acceptable\",\n        \"Works in Chrome 130+, Safari TP, Firefox Nightly as of 2025\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-189\",\n      \"title\": \"Use <dialog closedby='any'> for light-dismiss modals without JavaScript\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"Chrome 133+ adds the closedby attribute to the native <dialog> element, enabling backdrop-click dismiss declaratively without JavaScript event listeners. Reduces bundle size and improves accessibility reliability for cookie consent, gallery lightbox, and booking modals.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Cookie consent, gallery lightbox, and booking confirmation modals use <dialog closedby='any'>\",\n        \"Escape key closes all dialogs without additional JS handler\",\n        \"Clicking backdrop closes dialogs where closedby='any' is set\",\n        \"Progressive enhancement: feature detection used for graceful fallback\",\n        \"Screen readers announce dialog correctly via native dialog role\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/blog/dialog-closedby\",\n        \"Combine with ::backdrop CSS for branded overlay\",\n        \"Remove duplicate JS click-outside listeners after migration\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-190\",\n      \"title\": \"Add SiteNavigationElement schema to main navigation for Google Sitelinks\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"Google Search supports schema.org SiteNavigationElement to understand a site's primary navigation structure. Adding this to the main navigation helps Google understand site hierarchy and can improve Sitelinks display in SERPs for branded searches.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"JSON-LD script in layout.tsx includes SiteNavigationElement for all primary nav items\",\n        \"Each item has @type: SiteNavigationElement, name, and url properties\",\n        \"Rich Results Test validates the schema without errors\",\n        \"Navigation items in schema match exactly the visible nav links\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Reference: https://schema.org/SiteNavigationElement\",\n        \"Use ItemList wrapping SiteNavigationElement for ordered nav\",\n        \"Combine with existing WebSite SearchAction schema in the same JSON-LD block\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-191\",\n      \"title\": \"Comply with Malaysia CPETTR 2024 — mandatory Bahasa Malaysia disclosure\",\n      \"priority\": \"critical\",\n      \"description\": \"The Consumer Protection (Electronic Trade Transaction) Regulations 2024 came into force on 25 December 2024 and require all information shown to Malaysian consumers in online trade transactions to be available in Bahasa Malaysia. This includes pricing, descriptions, terms and conditions, and mandatory trader identity disclosures (name, address, registration, contact). Non-compliance exposes the business to enforcement under the Consumer Protection Act 1999.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"All price displays, room descriptions, booking terms, cancellation policy, and contact details are available in Bahasa Malaysia on the website\",\n        \"A Bahasa Malaysia toggle or dedicated BM version serves the required content (can be the same page with i18n)\",","numLines":100,"startLine":4200,"totalLines":6135}}}
